## Other sections (minimum bar)

| Section | Pass criteria |
|---------|----------------|
| Troubleshooting | Symptom \| Cause \| Fix table; topic-real failures |
| Common Mistakes | 2–4 `!!! warning` with Fix |
| Security | 5 topic-specific bullets |
| Best Practices | 5 actionable bullets |
| References | Official docs first |

Diagrams: **Excalidraw only** under `docs/assets/excalidraw/` (never D2/Mermaid for tutorials).

---

## Anti-patterns (fail review)

- Templated “Gather host baseline” labs for every Linux/Shell page  
- Identical Challenge text across a course  
- Placeholder commands (`# TODO`, `echo hello` as the whole lab)  
- Invented kubectl/terraform/aws flags  
- Interview Qs unrelated to the page Theory  
- D2 diagrams or stale `## Goal` / `{ .ra-facts }` tutorial skeletons  
- Marketing / buzzword padding  

---

## Done means

A stranger can:

1. Read Theory and understand the topic without another site.  
2. Paste lab commands and finish with a working result + evidence.  
3. Answer interview questions using only this page’s content.  

If any of those fail, the page is not done.
